# Stackra file contract:
# Purpose: who reviews which paths. GitHub requests a review from the owners of every file a pull
#          request touches, and the main ruleset (.github/rulesets/main.json) requires one of them to
#          approve.
# Boundary: path → owner only. The last matching line wins, so specific paths come after `*`.
# Runtime: node
# Governing contract: Stackra ADR 0158 (the committed manifests are contracts other members build
#                     from, https://docs.stackra.figentra.com/adr/0158-gen-artefacts-openapi-manifest-and-client)

# Everything defaults to the platform team.
* @acme/platform-team

# Decisions: the project's ADRs.
apps/docs/src/adr/ @acme/platform-team

# The contracts consumers generate their clients from.
**/.stackra/app-manifest.json @acme/platform-team
**/.stackra/openapi.json @acme/platform-team

# Infrastructure, environments and pinned producer revisions.
runway.yaml @acme/platform-team
stackra.lock.yaml @acme/platform-team

# CI, release, rulesets, issue and pull request templates.
.github/ @acme/platform-team

# Governance: versions, toolchain, task graph, hooks, secret scanning, release notes and the
# security policy.
pnpm-workspace.yaml @acme/platform-team
mise.toml @acme/platform-team
.node-version @acme/platform-team
turbo.jsonc @acme/platform-team
lefthook.yml @acme/platform-team
.gitleaks.toml @acme/platform-team
.changeset/ @acme/platform-team
SECURITY.md @acme/platform-team
